						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">In the wake of the Katrina disaster I feel very strongly that Americans have there head in the sand.&nbsp; It took four days to get relief workers to get to the New Orleans Dome to evacuate 3,000 people.&nbsp; Not only that but it will take 6 months for New Orleans waters to recede and another 3 months for New Orleans to dry out.&nbsp; We have not had a war on our land since the civil war, what is going to happen if we are faced with a nuclear or chemical attack that destroys a city. Are we prepared ?&nbsp; No we arent!!!!!&nbsp; What if we are attacked by air are we safe??&nbsp; No we arent!!!! Are we prepared for famine or drought like we had in the 30&#039;s and 40&#039;s (dust bowl)? No we arent.&nbsp; Americans have it very nice here rich or poor we have food and water and we take care of our homeless, we even have shelters for the homeless.&nbsp; But we cannot take care of a City that needs it. We are ready to jump a mile high for other countries but we do nothing for our people?&nbsp; Its a DISGRACE!! Its EMBARRASSING!!&nbsp; It took a good SWIFT KICK IN THE PANTS for our President to get aid down there.&nbsp; I voted for Bush and I dont blame him for the Hurricane,&nbsp; Presidents dont control the whether but Presidents do fund aid&nbsp; for relief for natural disasters!! I think all of us should start opening our eyes because we live in a DANGEROUS world and if we arent on our toes.. We could all have New Orleans in our town.&nbsp; &nbsp;I sincerely hope everyone donates to the Red Cross because one day it might be your town. Even 5 dollars or donate water would be sufficient.&nbsp; WE need to take care of our own!!! Sorry I just had to right something this just pisses me off alot as well it should for many people!<br /><br />Peace out <br /><br />Colleen Quickness</td>
